CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     The ssttrrppttiimmee() function assumes the Gregorian calendar and will produce
     incorrect results for dates prior to its introduction.

BBUUGGSS
     Both the _%_e and _%_l format specifiers may incorrectly scan one too many
     digits if the intended values comprise only a single digit and that digit
     is followed immediately by another digit.  Both specifiers accept zero-
     padded values, even though they are both defined as taking unpadded val‐
     ues.

     The _%_p format specifier has no effect unless it is parsed _a_f_t_e_r hour-re‐
     lated specifiers.  Specifying _%_l without _%_p will produce undefined re‐
     sults.  Note that 12AM (ante meridiem) is taken as midnight and 12PM
     (post meridiem) is taken as noon.

     The _%_Z format specifier only accepts time zone abbreviations of the local
     time zone, or the value "GMT".  This limitation is because of ambiguity
     due to of the over loading of time zone abbreviations.  One such example
     is _E_S_T which is both Eastern Standard Time and Eastern Australia Summer
     Time.

     The ssttrrppttiimmee() function does not correctly handle multibyte characters in
     the _f_o_r_m_a_t argument.

